Use this command only from an active `itldev/*` development branch worktree.

Run the helper from the current project directory:

<!-- ITL_LONG_RUN -->

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action export-dev-branch-result
```

Only an explicit human request to prepare for a working infobase adds `-ResultPurpose production`; otherwise keep the default intermediate export.

Under `VERIFICATION_POLICY=warn`, the helper warns and exports without confirmation. Under `VERIFICATION_POLICY=block`, it stops and `/itl-check` must run first. On success with a non-empty `userReport`, render that Russian Markdown report verbatim as one uninterrupted block; it contains the verification decision and full CF/CFE and manifest paths. After the report, add a short `## Итог задачи` section only when this current agent already has reliable context from the preceding task: state what changed, what was verified, and any remaining risks or incomplete work. Do not make another tool call to build that summary, infer it from the export report, Git, or diagnostics, or invent missing history. When reliable task context is unavailable, stop after the verbatim `userReport`. Do not paraphrase the report or read `console.log`. For failures, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath`.
